"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1K3S0527T1S0KYXT\",\"title\":\"Hampton Roads WAE Project — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"MARINE\",\"1,000Y+\",\"Hampton Roads WAE Project\",\"CREW Carbon\",\"ISSUED\",\"49.53\",\"BUFFER POOL\",\"0.991\",\"CREDITING PERIOD\",\"01 Jul 2025 to 30 Jun 2030\",\"Summary\"],\"issued_header\":\"49.53\",\"buffer_header\":\"0.991\",\"crediting\":\"01 Jul 2025 to 30 Jun 2030\",\"verifier\":\"350Solutions\",\"code\":\"ZTF7\",\"approval\":\"18 Dec 2025\",\"protocol_current\":\"Wastewater Alkalinity Enhancement v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":\"49.53\",\"cert_retired\":\"0\",\"cert_buffer\":\"0.991\",\"reversal\":\"The risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to CREW Carbon's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 0.991 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 28.495 certificates.\\n\\nCREW Carbon has no reversals to date.\",\"showing\":[\"Showing 4 of 4\",\"Showing 1 of 1\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"18 Dec 2025\",\"Verification Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"18 Dec 2025\",\"GHG Statement Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"13 Nov 2025\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"14 Oct 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Issue date\",\"Issued\",\"Buffer pool\",\"Supplier allocation\"],\"rows\":[[\"18 Dec 2025\",\"49.53\",\"0.991\",\"48.539\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3\",\"t\":\"CREW Carbon\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/wastewater-alkalinity-enhancement/1.1\",\"t\":\"Wastewater Alkalinity Enhancement v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1K3S0527T1S0KYXT/pjd_1K7J80M9C1S07ME6/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 14 Oct 2025\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KAM1S37H1S0GDZR?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1K3S0527T1S0KYXT/pjd_1KCSQTVAD1S0DC98/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1K3S0527T1S0KYXT/pjd_1KCSNVFES1S0742W/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1K3S0527T1S0KYXT/pjd_1KATSEKBN1S064G9/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1K3S0527T1S0KYXT/pjd_1K7J80M9C1S07ME6/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nMARINE\\n1,000Y+\\nHampton Roads WAE Project\\nCREW Carbon\\nISSUED\\n49.53\\nBUFFER POOL\\n0.991\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Jul 2025 to 30 Jun 2030\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nCREW removes carbon dioxide from the atmosphere by deploying fine-grained natural minerals like calcium carbonate in wastewater treatment systems. The deployment location for this project includes wastewater facilities operated by the Hampton Roads Sanitation District (“HRSD”), a political subdivision of the Commonwealth of Virginia, serving the Hampton Roads region.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nZTF7\\nApproval date\\n18 Dec 2025\\nCurrent protocol version\\nWastewater Alkalinity Enhancement v1.1\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nHampton Roads WAE Project\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nMarine carbon dioxide removal (mCDR) leverages the ocean's natural capacity to absorb and store carbon for thousands of years. These pathways use the biogeochemical and physical properties of the ocean and other bodies of water to capture carbon dioxide from the atmosphere or to permanently store carbon already contained within them. Approaches to mCDR include Ocean Alkalinity Enhancement and Direct Ocean Capture and Storage.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n14 Oct 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 49.53 tCO₂e removed from Hampton Roads WAE Project on 26 Oct 2025\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n49.532 t\\nSequestrations\\n79.922 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n28.981 tCO₂e\\n-\\nUncertainty Discount\\n1.410 t\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n18 Dec 2025\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n18 Dec 2025\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n13 Nov 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n14 Oct 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n49.53\\nRetired\\n0\\nBuffer pool\\n0.991\\nCrediting period\\n01 Jul 2025 to 30 Jun 2030\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n18 Dec 2025\\t49.53\\t0.991\\t48.539\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to CREW Carbon's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 0.991 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 28.495 certificates.\\n\\nCREW Carbon has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"